Eyeliner — a Yapfast theme

1. The theme itself — theme.json, the pictures in art/, previews/ and icon.png,
   the cursors in cursors/ and the sounds in sounds/ — is dedicated to the public
   domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
   Every collage element (crosses, stars, hearts, bats, bows, flowers, bokeh,
   checker scraps, scrawled words), the winged heart, chain, blinkie stamps and
   cursors were drawn by scripts written for this theme; every sound was
   synthesised from sine partials, noise and a plucked-string model by a script
   written for this theme. No outside images or recordings are used.

2. The icons in icons/ are Yapfast's stock icons re-drawn as marker solids for
   this theme (each shape rasterised, thickened, given one shared hand wobble and
   traced back to a path). They are adaptations, so they keep their sources'
   licences:
   - Most come from Solar by 480 Design, under CC BY 4.0
     (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), via Iconify, as listed in
     Yapfast's ui/icons/README.md. Changes: re-drawn in a marker style.
   - calendar, check, chevron-down, chevron-left, chevron-right, hand, maximize,
     minimize, minus, restore, slash, square, x, forward and reply come from
     Lucide (https://lucide.dev/), under the ISC licence:
       ISC License. Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by Cole Bemis
       2013-2022 as part of Feather (MIT). All other copyright (c) for Lucide
       are held by Lucide Contributors 2022.
       Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any
       purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above
       copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.
       THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES.
   - The icons drawn for Yapfast itself (see its ui/icons/README.md) are
     re-drawn here under the same terms as Yapfast's own.
   - pin.svg, pin-off.svg (a safety pin) and logo.svg (a winged heart) are new
     drawings for this theme, CC0.
   Discord's logo and the verified badge are not replaced; they stay stock.

3. The fonts in fonts/ are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; each family's
   licence is beside it (OFL-*.txt):
   - GrenzeGotisch.ttf — Grenze Gotisch, Copyright 2020 The Grenze Gotisch Project
     Authors. fonts/OFL-grenzegotisch.txt
   - HankenGrotesk.ttf — Hanken Grotesk, Copyright 2021 The Hanken Grotesk Project
     Authors. fonts/OFL-hankengrotesk.txt
   - JetBrainsMono.ttf — JetBrains Mono, Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project
     Authors. fonts/OFL-jetbrainsmono.txt
   All are shipped unmodified. The scrawled words in the collage and the blinkie
   lettering were set in Sedgwick Ave Display and Silkscreen (both OFL 1.1) and
   baked into the pictures; those fonts are not shipped.
